# Line-ending policy — deliberately committed, not left to local git config.
#
# Without this file, normalization depends on each contributor's `core.autocrlf`
# setting. That is a real hazard for THIS project: the content owner edits Bible
# JSON on Windows and publishes with `git add .` (docs/bible-editing-guide.md).
# On a machine where autocrlf is not enabled, an editor saving CRLF would turn a
# one-verse correction into a whole-file rewrite — a ~31,000-line diff that
# buries the actual change and makes review impossible.
#
# `text=auto` stores every text file with LF in the repository regardless of the
# platform it was authored on, while leaving the working copy native. The result
# is deterministic history on every machine, with no setup step to remember.
* text=auto

# Binary assets must never be normalized — doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.tar.gz binary
